<h1>Lesson 4: Advanced Algorithms</h1>
<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 8-12</div>
<p>This module offers a brief overview of the key concepts and teaching strategies in each lesson, it isn't a replacement for reviewing each lesson in full before you teach it. Take your time with the individual lesson plans for a deeper dive.</p>
<p>This lesson prepares you to teach five curriculum lessons:</p>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 8:</b> Introduction to Loops</p>
<a href="[LESSON 8 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 8</a>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 9:</b> Conditional Statements</p>
<a href="[LESSON 9 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 9</a>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 10:</b> Algorithms IRL</p>
<a href="[LESSON 10 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 10</a>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 11:</b> Decomposition</p>
<a href="[LESSON 11 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 11</a>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 12:</b> Two-Way Selection</p>
<a href="[LESSON 12 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 12</a>
</div>
<hr>
<p><b>By the end of this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Explore how while loops repeat instructions while a condition remains true</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• See how if and if/else statements let a program make decisions between one or two outcomes</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Practice breaking down problems using flowcharts before implementing them in code</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Preview how algorithms show up in real-world contexts, including where fairness and bias can enter algorithmic decisions</p>
<p style="margin: 16px 0 0 0;"><i>Suggested time: 25 minutes</i></p>
<hr>
